1. **[MAJOR] [THEORY:228](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/THEORY.md:228)** \(D\) is a utility-valued *perfect-information value for observing the state*; entropy reduction is a different functional, not the same quantity converted from nats. Also, [MES targets the optimum **value**](https://arxiv.org/abs/1703.01968), whereas [ES](https://arxiv.org/abs/1112.1217) and [PES](https://arxiv.org/abs/1406.2541) target its location. **Fix:** Describe a decision-theoretic analogy, distinguish the targets, and remove the claimed unit conversion in the outline and exploration record.
2. **[MAJOR] [THEORY:257](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/THEORY.md:257)** [GP-Hedge](https://mwhoffman.com/papers/hoffman_2011.pdf) updates every acquisition arm using the updated GP posterior mean at its nominated point, not each arm’s realized terminal gain. P3 addresses a specified two-arm router; the observed frontier does not measure its per-state premise. **Fix:** Correct the reward description and limit P3’s portfolio comparison to an analogy.
3. **[MAJOR] [THEORY:166](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/THEORY.md:166)** Axis-aligned trees *can represent* the rule, but coverage and no aliasing do not guarantee that a trained random forest learns the exact partition or that correct trees dominate its average. **Fix:** State L1 as a representability result with explicit fitted-tree conditions; retain exact imitation as an empirical observation.
4. **[MINOR] [THEORY:244](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/THEORY.md:244)** The GP posterior summarizes observations under a specified model, while process decisions also depend on budget, configuration, and execution state; the E1 probe does not establish a near-lossless projection. **Fix:** Narrow both sufficiency and “near-lossless” to the measured label-prediction task.

The Howard 1966, Lindley 1956, Raiffa–Schlaifer 1961, Mockus 1978, Srinivas 2010, Hoffman–Brochu–de Freitas 2011, Hennig–Schuler 2012, Hernández-Lobato 2014, Wang–Jegelka 2017, and LMABO ICLR 2026 attributions are otherwise reasonable. [Howard’s paper](https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/4082064/) specifically distinguishes decision value from information measured only by probabilities.

### D. Positioning fairness — REVISE

1. **[MAJOR] [exploration_rounds:36](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/ref_papers/exploration_rounds.md:36)** “No cost governance” overstates the LMABO distinction: [LMABO reports roughly 6,000 tokens, about $0.01, and latency per iteration](https://proceedings.iclr.cc/paper_files/paper/2026/file/f1b7a29fe9759d4c9d23f78738e40b42-Paper-Conference.pdf), though it does not optimize a quality–cost routing frontier. **Fix:** Use that narrower distinction; describe this paper’s menu as *broader process actions* rather than implying LMABO has no strategy-level controller.

### E. Exploration priorities — REVISE

1. **[MAJOR] [exploration_rounds:33](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/ref_papers/exploration_rounds.md:33)** “GP-Hedge-over-8-actions, updated by terminal gain” is not a defined GP-Hedge baseline here: the menu includes stop and refit actions, terminal feedback is delayed and observed only for the chosen trajectory, and GP-Hedge’s full-information posterior-mean reward applies to acquisition nominees. **Fix:** Make accurate GP-Hedge scoping P0; specify a comparable acquisition-only baseline or a separately named, fully specified strategy-level bandit before requiring an experiment. [GP-Hedge algorithm](https://mwhoffman.com/papers/hoffman_2011.pdf).

