A1 — **PARTIALLY** — The abstract is much shorter, but lines 44–62 contain **210 whitespace-delimited words**, exceeding its ≤200-word heading. [Outline](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/workshop_paper_outline.md:42)

A2 — **ADDRESSED** — The §4 limitation now says the *transfer comparison* is one-step and acknowledges the separate closed-loop RF evaluation in §6.5. [Outline](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/workshop_paper_outline.md:335)

A3 — **ADDRESSED** — P3 calls the sweep “CONSISTENT with” its premise and says \(A(s)\) was not measured. [Outline](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/workshop_paper_outline.md:223)

A4 — **ADDRESSED** — The §4 subsections are numbered 4.1 and 4.2; the checked references say “limitation 9/15.” [Outline](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/workshop_paper_outline.md:349)

A5 — **ADDRESSED** — The test-count history now gives 385 → 421 → 423, including the final two additions. [Outline](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/workshop_paper_outline.md:811)

B1 — **ADDRESSED** — The outline gives BT as positive on 5/5 and proper-score as positive on 3/5, negative on Branin and Hartmann, in both streams; the values match the two saved JSON files. [Outline](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/workshop_paper_outline.md:391)

B2 — **ADDRESSED** — Limitation 3 and [PROGRESS_BRANCH.md](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/PROGRESS_BRANCH.md:430) give 4 global→surrogate, 1 local→surrogate, and 1 global→local, matching the Lenz-branch report read via `git show`. [Outline](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/workshop_paper_outline.md:691)

B3 — **ADDRESSED** — The replication pooled proper-score delta is +0.052, consistent with the saved value 0.052497 at three decimals. [Outline](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/workshop_paper_outline.md:401)

B4 — **ADDRESSED** — The text says the broad strong/small grouping replicates and explicitly notes that the top two exchange places. [Outline](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/workshop_paper_outline.md:405)

C1 — **PARTIALLY** — [THEORY.md](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/THEORY.md:234) and [outline §2](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/workshop_paper_outline.md:116) distinguish decision value from entropy reduction and ES/PES location from MES value. The [exploration record](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/ref_papers/exploration_rounds.md:19) still calls P2 a unit conversion.

C2 — **ADDRESSED** — GP-Hedge’s reward is described as the updated posterior mean for every nominated arm; P3 is explicitly limited to an analogy. [THEORY.md](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/THEORY.md:272)

C3 — **ADDRESSED** — Both the [L1 proposition](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/THEORY.md:164) and [classical-relation bullet](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/THEORY.md:287) state representability and separate it from the fitted forest’s empirical imitation.

C4 — **ADDRESSED** — Posterior sufficiency is model-conditional; the projection claim is scoped to predicting action labels with the tested features. [THEORY.md](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/THEORY.md:255)

D1 — **ADDRESSED** — Both files say LMABO reports cost but does not optimize the quality–cost frontier. [Exploration rounds](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/ref_papers/exploration_rounds.md:40), [model interaction survey](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/ref_papers/model_interaction_survey.md:120)

E1 — **PARTIALLY** — The [P0 item](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/ref_papers/exploration_rounds.md:33) correctly rejects GP-Hedge over all eight actions, but its Exp3 example still says a specification must be written before implementation. The [survey](/home/lcy/Documents/projects/opt_agent_v3/docs/ref_papers/model_interaction_survey.md:133) also retains the old GP-Hedge-over-8-actions proposal.

**VERDICT: REVISE**
